This product includes software developed by the volcano engine reinforcement
learning team at ByteDance:

    verl: a flexible, efficient and production-ready RL training library
          for large language models
    https://github.com/volcengine/verl
    Apache License 2.0

The AntiSD codebase is a fork of verl with additions in the following areas:

  * verl/workers/actor/dp_actor.py
        — `grpo_ca` loss path: PRM construction, JSD-unbiased forward,
          adaptive u-clip, teacher-perplexity λ controller with Schmitt
          hysteresis, length mask.
  * verl/workers/config/actor.py
        — CCIRConfig and SelfDistillationConfig dataclasses.
  * verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py
        — `_maybe_build_self_distillation_batch`: self-distillation rollout
          construction (group-wise solution selection, budget-aware
          truncation, environment-feedback templates, multi-turn /
          system-prefix / suffix reprompt styles).
  * verl/trainer/ppo/core_algos.py
        — `compute_self_distillation_loss`: full-logit / top-K teacher
          distillation losses.
  * recipe/antisd/
        — nine launch scripts reproducing the paper's main results
          (3 base models × 3 methods).
  * data/
        — dataset preprocessing scripts for DAPO-Math, deepmath, AIME 2024 /
          2025, HMMT 2025, BeyondAIME.

All other files retain their original copyright notices and license terms
from upstream verl. See `LICENSE` for the Apache 2.0 license text.

The original SDPO branding (folder names, internal experiment tags) has been
removed from documentation; the algorithm is referred to throughout as AntiSD
(Anti-Self-Distillation).
